        "draft": true,
        "body": "G08 adds an opt-in one-step wait so an NPC can pause and resume the same session without resetting budgets. It also binds restored CLI providers to saved configuration and verifies experiments from raw responses, fresh Engine command execution, and request ledgers.\n\nIndependent acceptance at 20f8f0f:\n- Windows Node 20.19.2: 408/408 tests; golden 12/12.\n- The legal, failed, and live batches verify with expected exit codes 0/1/0. Corrupted command and cost records are rejected; read-only checks leave evidence unchanged.\n- Eight recorded live requests all chose eat. Total cost: 5336 tokens; messages off 2102 / on 3234. Ledger latency: 299404 ms total, observed on shared GPUs.\n- Saved thinking=false and timeout=777 ms were independently exercised with local fake HTTP; step/run failures preserve the original error and authoritative state.\n\nScope: this proves the implemented mechanism and the recorded first-decision experiment. It does not establish cooperation or live continuation after wait. Defaults remain legacy/messages off.\n\nFollow-up: interrupted-cost reporting should count spent from begin reservations rather than completed finishes. The recorded eight requests all completed, so this does not affect this batch or the actual hard budget. Track the correction with the next bounded task; do not rerun G08 live.\n\nThis PR is stacked on codex/g07-player-messages (G07-R1 d41940d). Draft for owner review; no merge requested.",
